<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 07-AUG.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 07-AUG.</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Tina continues northward in the East China Sea. Tina is centered 300 miles south of Cheju, South Korea, moving north at 10 mph. Top winds are 85 mph. Tina is expected to weaken below typhoon strength before crossing over or close to Cheju in 24 hours and reaching mainland South Korea in 30 hours. Tina will bring heavy rain and gusty winds and should cause moderate damage.</p>
<p>Heavy rain and thunderstorms in Bangladesh the next few days may lead to further flooding resulting in crop and property damage.</p>
<p>Nothing further at this time.</p>
</text>
